# Cloudflare Workers RUNTIME secrets for local `wrangler dev`.
# Copy to .dev.vars (gitignored) and fill in. These are read per request by the
# SSR routes through `cloudflare:workers`, NOT at build time - build-time Sanity
# vars live in .env.
#
# In production these are set with `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>` (or in the
# Cloudflare dashboard under the Worker's Variables & Secrets).

# The token the live draft preview reads Sanity with. A VIEWER (read) token is
# enough; nothing in the preview path writes. Create at sanity.io/manage ->
# project xp3elugr -> API -> Tokens.
#
# Two names are accepted and whichever is set wins:
#   SANITY_TOKEN           - the name the rest of the site family uses
#   SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN  - the name this project already uses for its Worker
# If SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN is already a Worker secret in production, the preview
# comes up with no new secret to set.
#
# WRITE THE VALUE BARE. A quoted token yields a 401 that reads like a permissions
# problem (see the gotchas in CLAUDE.md).
SANITY_TOKEN=

# ── Quote form Worker (already required by POST /api/quote) ────────────────────
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# QUOTE_OWNER_EMAIL=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
